Hi,

by asking you to create a MyGenomeInformation and test your file with
it was to make sure your file was in the correct format and could be
read by the package.  I noticed from your other email that you managed
to incorporate it by renaming the file.  However, there is now a more
standard/generic way to do it, which does not involve having to setup
a MyGenomeInformation class.

The new solution is to create a so called UGP (Unit Genome Position)
file and import your existing annotation data into that.  See group
page "Unit Genome Position (UGP) files" for an example how to import
data from a tabular file, which is quite easy:

http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/web/unit-genome-position-ugp-files

You know you've got a working UGP file, when you can do things like this:

> chipType <- "GenomeWideSNP_6";
> ugp <- AromaUgpFile$fromChipType(chipType);
> print(ugp)

